From f33c23cb832b725f4c3814137177377d62b26ec5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Josef Schlehofer <pepe.schlehofer@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 06:15:25 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] mac80211: realtek: add pending fixes for 2.4 GHz AP on
 RTL8822BU

Add two pending rtw88 fixes for a TP-Link Archer T4U v3 (RTL8812BU,
handled by rtw_8822bu) running as a 2.4 GHz AP.

Under ETSI, rtw88 sets the RTL8822B EDCCA threshold to min(IGI, 36),
at most about -74 dBm. In-band energy, mostly from the adapter's own
USB 3 link, kept it at 36, and the AP was not seen in any of 5 scans.
The first patch uses the normal threshold, max(IGI + 8, 48), on 2.4 GHz
under ETSI, capped at 50 (nominally -60 dBm), and keeps the existing
rule on 5 GHz and in JP. With it, the AP was seen in 4 of 5 scans.

Over USB, the reserved page with the beacon is only queued before
BCN_VALID is polled, so the poll can time out, which logs "error beacon
valid" and "failed to download drv rsvd page" (lwfinger/rtw88#451).
v5 of the second patch waits for that URB and kills it if it does not
complete within 5 s. It is acked by the rtw88 maintainer and is
independent of 052, which disables the beacon function during the
upload.

Both were tested with backports 7.2 on main on a Turris 1.x. For the
USB patch this was v4 (v5 only reorders declarations, drops an
initializer and rewords a comment): the AP came up after each of 15
restarts without beacon errors, but the build without it did not log
them either, so this only shows no regression.

Only the line numbers are adapted to backports 6.12.96;
secs_to_jiffies() is provided by kernel 6.6.157. Build-tested for
mpc85xx/p2020.

Link: https://lore.kernel.org/all/20261011204509.46062-1-pepe.schlehofer@gmail.com/
Link: https://lore.kernel.org/all/20261013033737.6761-1-pepe.schlehofer@gmail.com/
Link: https://github.com/openwrt/openwrt/pull/25836
Link: https://github.com/openwrt/openwrt/pull/25837
Signed-off-by: Josef Schlehofer <pepe.schlehofer@gmail.com>
---
